  "question": {
    "text": "A monochromatic light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6000</mn><mo> </mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mover></math> is incident on the single slit of width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo> </mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. If the diffraction pattern is formed at the focus of the convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo> </mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, the linear width of the central maximum is :",
